lesson: 254
title: Pizzas and cakes for a crowd
level: primary-4
stars: 1
explain: A large pizza is cut into 8 slices.
explain: To find how many pizzas to order, count all the slices people will eat, then see how many pizzas of 8 that needs.
explain: If the slices do not fill the last pizza, you still need one more whole pizza: 9 children × 2 slices = 18 slices; 2 pizzas give 16, too few, so order 3.
vars: a=name b=name c=3..20 k=2..3
let: s = c * k
answer: (s + 7 - (s + 7) % 8) / 8
exercise: {c} children at {a}'s party each eat {k} slices of large pizza. How many large pizzas must be ordered?
exercise: {a}'s team has {c} players, and each player wants {k} slices of large pizza. How many large pizzas are needed?
exercise: For movie night, {c} friends will eat {k} slices of large pizza each. What is the smallest number of large pizzas {a} should buy?
exercise: The class orders large pizzas for {c} pupils. Every pupil gets {k} slices. How many large pizzas does the class order?
exercise: {a} and {b} invite {c} guests, and each guest will have {k} slices of large pizza. How many large pizzas must they get?
exercise: {c} kids, {k} slices each, how many large pizzas do we order
exercise: ordering pizza for {c+1}, no sorry {c} people, {k} slices a head. how many large ones
exercise: footy party, {c} of us n everyone eats {k} slices, {a}'s mum bringing the drinks. how many large pizzas
exercise: {c} mates over, each gonna eat {k} slices. how many large pizzas do i need
exercise: sleepover with {c} girls, {k} slices each yeah, how many big pizzas
test: What is the least number of large pizzas that gives {c} children {k} slices each?
test: Every one of {c} campers will eat {k} slices of large pizza. How many large pizzas does the camp leader need to order so nobody goes short?
test: {a} wants enough large pizzas for {c} people to have {k} slices apiece. How many pizzas is that?
test: {c} hungry kids, {k} slices each. large pizzas needed?
test: {a} says {c} large pizzas for {c} kids eating {k} slices each. way too many. how many do we actually need
test: party for {c}, {k} slices a person, {b} doesn't like olives btw. how many large pizzas to order
exam: It is given that {c.words} children are each to consume {k.words} slices of large pizza. Determine the minimum number of large pizzas to be procured.
exam: A function is to be catered for {c} attendees, each of whom shall receive {k} slices of large pizza. Ascertain the least quantity of large pizzas sufficient for this purpose.
exam: Compute the smallest number of large pizzas whose slices suffice to provide {k} slices in respect of each of {c} guests.
exam: Whereas {c} participants require {k} slices of large pizza apiece, state the minimum number of whole large pizzas that must be ordered.
exercise: {c+1} children were invited to {a}'s party, but {b} is under the weather and stays at home. Each child who comes eats {k} slices of large pizza. How many large pizzas must be ordered?
exercise: {c} of us at {a}'s, and {b} says {b.he}'s watching {b.his} weight, yeah right, {b.he}'ll scoff {k} slices like everyone else. how many large pizzas do we order?
test: {a}'s team of {c} had a disappointing result (they lost nine nil), but each player still wants {k} slices of large pizza. How many large pizzas will feed them?
